{"name":"Silent Film","hex":"#9fa5a5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silent film","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A film with no synchronized recorded sound, especially spoken dialogue."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silent_film"}],"entries":[{"title":"Silent film","blocks":[{"text":"A silent film is a film without synchronized recorded sound. Though silent films convey narrative and emotion visually, various plot elements or key lines of dialogue may, when necessary, be conveyed by the use of intertitles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Tango_scene_from_The_Four_Horsemen_of_the_Apocalypse.jpg/330px-Tango_scene_from_The_Four_Horsemen_of_the_Apocalypse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silent_film"},{"title":"Film","blocks":[{"text":"A film, movie, or motion picture is a work of visual art that simulates experiences and otherwise communicates ideas, stories, perceptions, emotions, or atmosphere through the use of moving images that are generally, since the 1930s, synchronized with sound and sometimes feature other sensory stimuli."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Le_Voyage_dans_la_Lune_%281902%29.webm/330px--Le_Voyage_dans_la_Lune_%281902%29.webm.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Film"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Horse_in_Motion_-_Sallie_Gardner_%28animation%29.gif/500px-Horse_in_Motion_-_Sallie_Gardner_%28animation%29.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Horse_in_Motion_-_Sallie_Gardner_%28animation%29.gif/500px-Horse_in_Motion_-_Sallie_Gardner_%28animation%29.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Animation of 11 frames of Eadweard Muybridge's 1878 cabinet